From 12b6ba369cb9a863e394b67a40ddcd15099b5426 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Emergent Agent <agent@emergent.local>
Date: Wed, 22 Jul 2026 19:32:04 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] fix(walk): render local-time static greeting + reset session on Done

Build 26B UX follow-up (frontend-only). Walk V5 intentionally removed the
AI-generated opener from /session/start; the frontend was still seeding the
transcript with an empty assistant bubble, producing a blank landing screen.

Changes (single file: frontend/app/walk-conversation.tsx):
  * Add client-only getLocalTimeGreeting() (morning / afternoon / evening).
  * Mount effect no longer inserts an empty opener when opening_message === "".
  * Render a static greeting hero (testID='walk-static-greeting') when
    phase === 'ready' && messages.length === 0 && streamBuffer.length === 0.
    Never persisted, never sent to the backend, disappears the moment the
    user's first message hits the transcript.
  * Gate 'Close this conversation' on messages.some(m => m.role === 'user')
    so the button only appears once the user has spoken.
  * New handleDone: aborts any in-flight stream, clears all local session
    state (sessionId / messages / streamBuffer / candidates / savedFromExtraction
    / savedIds / error / pendingText), recomputes the greeting, then
    router.replace('/(tabs)/walk') — deterministic even for deep-link users
    with no back stack.
  * V4 fallback preserved: if opening_message is truthy, the transcript is
    still seeded with it as before.

No Walk V5 backend files touched. 196 python tests pass, testing_agent 12/12
Walk regression sweep passes.

